    "q-69022": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69022",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Marcel can transcribe $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a paper in $3$ hours. How many hours does it take him to transcribe $5$ papers?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the number of hours Marcel takes to transcribe $5$ papers, we can first find the unit rate of hours per paper, and then multiply the unit rate by $5$ papers.\n\nTo find the unit rate of hours per paper, we divide the number of hours, $3,$ by the number of papers, $\\frac{3}{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{3}{8}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3÷\\frac{3}{8} & =3\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 8}{1\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3} \\\\  & =24÷3 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $8$ hours per paper. To find the number of hours that Marcel takes to transcribe $5$ papers, we multiply the unit rate by $5$ papers and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\times 5 & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Marcel can transcribe $5$ papers in $40$ hours.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
