    "q-148226": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148226",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Laura can decorate $5$ cakes in $\\frac{5}{2}$ hours. How many cakes can she decorate in $3$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the number of cakes Laura can decorate in $3$ hours, we first find the unit rate of cakes per hour and then multiply it by $3$ hours.\n\nTo find the unit rate of cakes per hour, we divide the number of cakes, $5,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{5}{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n5÷\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5÷\\frac{5}{2} & =5\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1}\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\times 2}{1\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =10÷5 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $2$ cakes per hour. To determine the number of cakes Laura can decorate in $3$ hours, we multiply the unit rate by $3$ hours and get\n\n$$\n2\\times 3=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Laura can decorate $6$ cakes in $3$ hours.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
