    "q-148285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148285",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "To make a cake mix, Eva uses $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a cup of wheat flour and $\\frac{3}{16}$ of a cup of sugar. How many cups of flour does she need if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar?",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the number of cups of flour Eva needs if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar, we first find the unit ratio of cups of flour per cup of sugar and then multiply it by $2$ cups of sugar.\n\nTo find the unit ratio of cups of flour per cup of sugar, we divide the number of cups of flour, $\\frac{3}{8},$ by the number of cups of sugar, $\\frac{3}{16},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{3}{16}\n$$\n\nDividing one fraction by another is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{3}{16} & =\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 16}{8\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{24} \\\\  & =48÷24 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $2$ cups of flour per cup of sugar. To determine the number of cups of flour Eva needs if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar, we multiply the unit rate by $2$ cups of sugar and get\n\n$$\n2\\times 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Eva needs $4$ cups of flour if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
